      "lyric": "[Verse 1]\nThey took the chairs from the folding hall\nLeft one bent leg by the bathroom wall\nI held your coat when you said goodbye\nLike a fool keeps time while the years go by\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nYou said, “Don’t wait up, the road runs fast”\nI heard the door, then I heard the past\n\n[Chorus]\nI’m still here, still here, where you left me\nSame old floor, same cheap light overhead\nYou got clear, got clear, got free\nI got your name like a stone in my teeth\nStill here, still here, say it louder\nIf I’m lost, let the lost be proud\nYou moved on, but I won’t disappear\nI’m still here, still here, still here\n\n[Verse 2]\nYour mother calls on a Sunday noon\nAsks if I’ve heard from you lately too\nI say, “We’re fine,” and I bite my tongue\nThat little lie is the sharpest one\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nThe train went north, the platform shook\nI watched your face, but you never looked\n\n[Chorus]\nI’m still here, still here, where you left me\nSame old floor, same cheap light overhead\nYou got clear, got clear, got free\nI got your name like a stone in my teeth\nStill here, still here, say it louder\nIf I’m lost, let the lost be proud\nYou moved on, but I won’t disappear\nI’m still here, still here, still here\n\n[Bridge]\n(Oh-oh, let it hurt, let it hurt)\nI was the hand beneath your weight\nThe open door, the borrowed faith\nYou called it love, then called it late\nNow I call my own name\n\n[Breakdown]\nNo more waiting by the phone\nNo more making your leaving home\nNo more mercy dressed as blame\nI survived the shape you gave my name\n\n[Final Chorus]\nI’m still here, still here, and you can hear me\nNot your ghost, not your spare, not your shame\nYou got clear, got clear, got free\nI got blood, I got breath, I got me\nStill here, still here, sing it louder\nFrom the floor to the last high cloud\nYou moved on, but I won’t disappear\nI’m still here, still here, still here\n\n[Outro]\nStill here\nStill here\nYou left me there\nI found me here",
