      "style": "variety 1/4, emotionally direct contemporary pop, midtempo pulse, close dry lead vocal, restrained piano and muted guitar in the verses, tight kick and warm bass entering at the pre-chorus, wide stacked harmonies and fuller drums in the chorus, a brief stripped bridge, clean polished mix with intimate vocal detail, cathartic sing-along hook, strong rhythmic repetition and open vowel phrasing",
      "lyric": "[Verse 1]\nYou took the boxes, left the key\nLeft one blue cup here for me\nThe movers laughed, the hallway shook\nI stood there like an afterthought\n\nYou said, \"You'll find your way somehow\"\nI nodded then, I don't know how\nThe elevator closed its doors\nYour life went up, mine stayed on the floor\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI keep the light on by the sink\nI hear your voice before I think\nEverybody says, \"Move along\"\nBut moving on feels like moving wrong\n\n[Chorus]\nI got left behind, left behind\nWatching your taillights turn to white\nYou got a head start, I got the night\nYou found a new road, I lost the signs\nI say I'm fine, fine, fine\nTill the word falls flat each time\nI got left behind, left behind\nAnd I still reach for your side\n\n[Verse 2]\nYour mother called me Sunday noon\nAsked if I had heard from you\nI said, \"We're good,\" I said, \"We're grown\"\nThen ate cold rice here alone\n\nThe calendar still marks the date\nLike paper knows what people take\nI crossed your name, then wrote it back\nSome little truths refuse to pack\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI wear the jacket that you left\nIt doesn't fit, but fits me best\nEverybody says, \"You'll be okay\"\nThey don't know what okay can weigh\n\n[Chorus]\nI got left behind, left behind\nWatching your taillights turn to white\nYou got a head start, I got the night\nYou found a new road, I lost the signs\nI say I'm fine, fine, fine\nTill the word falls flat each time\nI got left behind, left behind\nAnd I still reach for your side\n\n[Bridge]\n(Oh-oh, I know, I know)\nMaybe one day this room will breathe\nMaybe your leaving won't define me\nBut tonight, if I'm telling the truth\nI miss the life that ended with you\n\n[Final Chorus]\nI got left behind, left behind\nBut I can hear my own heart tonight\nNo head start, no borrowed sign\nI can take this long road one mile at a time\nI say I'm fine, fine, fine\nNot like before, but I might be right\nI got left behind, left behind\nStill here, still mine, still alive\n\n[Outro]\nStill here, still mine\nOne mile at a time",
