      "style": "Jazz, modern jazz ballad with a slow brushed swing, upright bass walking beneath sparse piano voicings and muted trumpet answering the vocal; close-miked smoky alto vocal, conversational verses opening into a singable repeated refrain, subtle call-and-response vocalese, restrained room ambience, warm organic mix, dynamic cathartic final chorus.\n\nTake 2: Jazz, modern jazz ballad; upright bass walking beneath sparse piano voicings, muted trumpet answering the vocal; slow brushed swing; close-miked vocals, restrained room ambience, warm organic mix; smoky alto with conversational verses, singable repeated refrain, subtle call-and-response vocalese, dynamic cathartic final chorus",
      "lyric": "[Verse 1]\nYou took the blue cup, left the cracked one here\nSaid, “Keep the change,” like change was cheap and clear\nThe train pulled out at quarter after two\nI watched the red tail lights forget about you\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI told the neighbors I was doing fine\nThen lost my place halfway through the line\n\n[Chorus]\nLeft behind, left behind\nI keep your leaving in the back of my mind\nYou crossed the door, I crossed the line\nLeft behind, left behind\n(oo-ah, oo-ah)\nI’m still arriving where you said goodbye\n\n[Verse 2]\nYour coat is gone, but one brass button stays\nCaught in the rug like it remembers days\nI sweep it up, then set it by the phone\nA little proof I wasn’t always alone\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nThe kettle cries, I let it cry awhile\nSome hurts get dressed and learn to wear a smile\n\n[Chorus]\nLeft behind, left behind\nI keep your leaving in the back of my mind\nYou crossed the door, I crossed the line\nLeft behind, left behind\n(oo-ah, oo-ah)\nI’m still arriving where you said goodbye\n\n[Bridge]\nDon’t tell me time is kind—it only moves\nIt takes the chairs, the names, the afternoon news\nAnd if I’m bitter, let the bitter be\nAt least this ache still answers back to me\n\n[Break]\nBa-da, ba-dee, ba-dah, stay\nBa-da, ba-dee, fade away\nNo, no, don’t dress it up tonight\nYou left; I stayed. That’s the whole damn fight.\n\n[Final Chorus]\nLeft behind, left behind\nI quit pretending I don’t mind\nYou crossed the door, I crossed the line\nLeft behind, left behind\n(oo-ah, oo-ah)\nI’m still arriving—\nStill arriving—\nStill arriving where you said goodbye\n\n[Outro]\nThe blue cup breaks. The morning comes.\nI say your name, then bite my tongue.",
