      "style": "Contemporary blues, weathered electric guitar bends, warm upright bass, restrained brushed drums and sparse piano answers; intimate raspy lead vocal with close conversational verses, wide sing-along chorus and call-and-response backing vocals; dry room sound with a gradual cathartic lift; slow 6/8 sway\n\nTake 2: Contemporary blues with an intimate raspy lead vocal, close conversational verses and a wide sing-along chorus with call-and-response backing vocals; dry room sound, gradual cathartic lift; weathered electric guitar bends, restrained brushed drums, warm upright bass, sparse piano answers; slow 6/8 sway, strong internal rhyme and repeated hook",
      "lyric": "[Verse 1]\nYou took the last train out at dawn,\nLeft your coffee cooling on,\nLeft your coat, left your key,\nLeft the leaving here with me.\n\nI said, “Go on, don’t turn around,”\nBut my brave words hit the ground.\nNow I wear what I can’t hide:\nYou got gone, and I stayed behind.\n\n[Chorus]\nI’m still here, still here,\nWith your goodbye ringing in my ear.\nStill here, still here,\nPaying for a promise you never kept near.\nYou moved on, I lost my ride—\nStill here, still here,\nOn the wrong side of goodbye.\n\n[Verse 2]\nYour sister called around noon,\nAsked if I had heard from you.\nI said, “No, but I’ll be fine,”\nLike a fool rehearsing a line.\n\nThere’s a dent beside the door,\nWhere you dropped your bag before.\nFunny how a little mark\nCan hold a whole house in the dark.\n\n[Chorus]\nI’m still here, still here,\nWith your goodbye ringing in my ear.\nStill here, still here,\nPaying for a promise you never kept near.\nYou moved on, I lost my ride—\nStill here, still here,\nOn the wrong side of goodbye.\n\n[Bridge]\nI don’t need your pity, no,\nI need the truth you wouldn’t show.\nIf I was easy to leave behind,\nSay it plain and let me mind.\n\n(Oh, let it ache, let it ache)\nI’d rather bleed than live half-awake.\n(Oh, let it break, let it break)\nSome hearts heal when the silence quits lying.\n\n[Final Chorus]\nI was still here, still here,\nBut I’m not yours to disappear.\nStill here, still here,\nTurning all this hurt into a voice you hear.\nYou moved on, I found my stride—\nStill here, still here,\nOn my own side of goodbye.\n\n[Outro]\nStill here, still here,\nNo more waiting by the door.\nStill here, still here,\nAin’t your leaving got me anymore.",
