      "style": "Country ballad, traditional roots production with natural room ambience, weathered acoustic guitar and restrained pedal steel, slow 6/8 sway with warm upright bass and brushed drums entering after the first chorus, intimate close-mic vocal, sparse verses, harmony-widened chorus, final chorus breaking into a raw held note\n\nTake 2: Country ballad, weathered acoustic guitar and restrained pedal steel, warm upright bass, traditional roots production with natural room ambience, slow 6/8 sway, brushed drums entering after the first chorus, intimate close-mic vocal, sparse verses, widening harmony chorus, raw held note in the final chorus",
      "lyric": "[Verse 1]\nYou took the blue suit from the closet\nLeft the work boots by the door\nSaid you needed room to breathe here\nLike you hadn't breathed before\nI stood still beside the coffee\nWhile the kettle cried its steam\nFunny how a house stays standing\nWhen it loses what it means\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI said, \"Go on, if you gotta go\"\nLike those words could make it true\nBut the hardest part of letting go\nIs knowing I was letting you\n\n[Chorus]\nYou got the leaving down to a science\nI got left with the why\nYou took the road past the county line\nAnd I took the long way through the night\nNow every door sounds like goodbye\nEvery chair still faces mine\nYou got the leaving down to a science\nI got left behind\n\n[Verse 2]\nYour mother called on Sunday\nAsked if you were doing well\nI said, \"He's fine,\" and watched the lie\nFall quiet as a bell\nThere's a dent beside the mattress\nWhere your shoulder used to be\nI keep sleeping near the edge now\nLike you're coming back for me\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI don't curse you, I don't bless you\nI just carry what you threw\nA heart can learn to beat alone\nBut it can't unlearn you\n\n[Chorus]\nYou got the leaving down to a science\nI got left with the why\nYou took the road past the county line\nAnd I took the long way through the night\nNow every door sounds like goodbye\nEvery chair still faces mine\nYou got the leaving down to a science\nI got left behind\n\n[Bridge]\n(Oh, I know, I know)\nThey say time will do its part\nBut time just teaches empty rooms\nTo recognize a breaking heart\nI can wash your cup, fold your shirt\nPut your picture out of sight\nBut I can't make this house believe\nYou didn't leave me here tonight\n\n[Final Chorus]\nYou got the leaving down to a science\nI got left with the why\nYou took the road past the county line\nAnd I took the long way through the night\nIf you ever turn that truck around\nDon't expect the porch light on\nYou got the leaving down to a science\nI got left—\n\n[Outro]\nLeft behind\nLeft behind\n(Still here, still here)\nLeft behind",
