      "style": "Modern cathartic metal, tight modern mix with harsh grit and clear vocal phrasing; crushing down-tuned guitars, bass locked to the riff, double-kick drums, brief clean-guitar breath before the final breakdown; stark intimate male vocals building into a raw roar; tense palm-muted verses opening into a wide anthemic chorus with relentless double-kick propulsion\n\nTake 2: Metal, tight modern mix with harsh grit and clear vocal phrasing, driving double-kick momentum, crushing down-tuned guitars with tense palm-muted verses and a brief clean-guitar breath before the final breakdown, bass locked to the riff, stark intimate male vocals building into a raw roar, wide anthemic chorus",
      "lyric": "[Verse 1]\nThey took the chairs when the sirens died\nLeft one coat on the other side\nI kept the key, I kept the scar\nThey drove away and called it far\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI said, “Wait up”—the road went black\nI learned the ones who leave don’t look back\n\n[Chorus]\nLeft me breathing, left me here\nWith the whole damn year inside my ear\nI was the hand beneath the wave\nYou were the crowd that walked away\nLeft me breathing, left me cold\nToo young to lose, too tired to hold\nIf I’m the proof that we survived\nWhy am I the one left outside?\n\n[Verse 2]\nYour mother said, “He’ll find his feet”\nLike feet can cross a flooded street\nI wore your name beneath my tongue\nA little prayer for what was young\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI said, “Come back”—the house stayed still\nSome doors are shut by someone else’s will\n\n[Chorus]\nLeft me breathing, left me here\nWith the whole damn year inside my ear\nI was the hand beneath the wave\nYou were the crowd that walked away\nLeft me breathing, left me cold\nToo young to lose, too tired to hold\nIf I’m the proof that we survived\nWhy am I the one left outside?\n\n[Bridge]\n(You don’t get to call this healing)\nWhen I’m the one who feels the ceiling\n(You don’t get to praise my fight)\nThen disappear before the night\nI carried water, I carried blame\nI carried every unsent name\nNow hear me plain, now hear me whole:\nYou left the body, not the soul\n\n[Breakdown]\nLeft—left—left me!\nStill here, still here!\nLeft—left—left me!\nSay it so the walls can hear!\n\n[Final Chorus]\nLeft me breathing, left me here\nBut I will not make a home of fear\nI was the hand beneath the wave\nI am the one I came to save\nLeft me breathing, left me cold\nNow I know what I can hold\nIf I’m the proof that we survived\nI’ll be the reason I stay alive\n\n[Outro]\nI stay alive\nI stay alive\nYou left me there\nI stayed alive",
