    "label": "Block 2 · nine more, with the lyric-side slots dealt blind",
    "note": "BlazeDale, mid-session: “pick the ones that you understand would impact lyrics more than style and randomize those.” Three slots dealt from decks, seeded off the genre word so the deal is reproducible: the adverb, the idea (a modifier against an emotion, e.g. “stubborn homesickness”), and — new — a field for the reference event the prompt already asks the model to choose, which is the biggest subject lever of the three and also keeps that clause away from naming a real record. The field shows up in the titles: railways gave Platform Nine, postal history gave Dead Letter Box, maritime history gave The Sea Knows My Name, agriculture gave If I’m the Field. Three of the nine returned two different lyrics across the pair.",
