      "describe": "While keeping things compelling, write tenderly prosed, emotive, and cathartic lyrics about something that would make the person with lived experience feel misplaced unease where the lyrics have exceptional Meter, Rhyme, repetition, and Rhythm in the spirit of techno while considering an apt metaphor, \"turn of phrase\", colloquialism, or idiom leaving the person with lived experience emotionally compelled by the lyrics that one cannot help but sing along due to the vowel juxtaposition even if sometimes those vowels are part of apt vocalese, all while reducing to the most poignant emotionality. To speak in a different voice or add vocal effect write within (). subtly vector the lyrics against a single reference event you creatively select from agriculture but ultimately the lyrics are only beholden to themselves. Get unvarnished with this one.",
      "style": "Melodic techno: four-on-the-floor kick, taut sub bass, clipped metallic percussion, restrained minor-key synth ostinato; dry spacious verses widening into a polished club mix; steady 124 BPM pulse; intimate close-miked lead vocal with doubled vowel tails, brief wordless vocalese, and a cathartic sing-along refrain.\n\nTake 2: Techno, melodic techno: four-on-the-floor pulse, taut sub bass, clipped metallic percussion, restrained minor-key synth ostinato; 124 BPM driving club tempo; dry spacious verses widening into a polished chorus mix; intimate close-miked lead vocal with doubled vowel tails and brief wordless vocalese, tightening into a cathartic sing-along refrain",
      "lyric": "[Verse 1]\nThey put my name on a weathered gate\nSaid, “Come on in, you’re home”\nBut every row ran straight and clean\nAnd still I walked alone\n\nThe wheat came up like little knives\nAgainst a borrowed sky\nI learned to smile, I learned the work\nI never learned the why\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI kept the measure, missed the mark\nI wore the dust like skin\nYou called it growing season\nI called it giving in\n\n[Chorus]\nI don’t belong where the harvest is high\nI don’t belong, but I still arrive\nHey-oh, hey-oh, carry me through\nIf I’m the field, what grew in you?\nI don’t belong—say it plain, say it slow\nI don’t belong, but I won’t let go\nAh-ah, oh-oh, under the blue\nIf I’m the field, what grew in you?\n\n[Verse 2]\nAt threshing time the whole town came\nWith silver in their hair\nThey praised the yield, they blessed the ground\nNobody saw me there\n\nI found one stalk beneath the floor\nBent double, split, and green\nI held it like a little proof\nThat breaking isn’t clean\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI kept the measure, missed the mark\nI wore the dust like skin\nYou called it growing season\nI called it giving in\n\n[Chorus]\nI don’t belong where the harvest is high\nI don’t belong, but I still arrive\nHey-oh, hey-oh, carry me through\nIf I’m the field, what grew in you?\nI don’t belong—say it plain, say it slow\nI don’t belong, but I won’t let go\nAh-ah, oh-oh, under the blue\nIf I’m the field, what grew in you?\n\n[Bridge]\nDon’t call me barren, don’t call me blessed\nI’m tired of names pinned to my chest\nThe earth can open, the earth can close\nA seed knows less than anybody knows\n\n[Break]\nAh-ah-ah, I still arrive\nOh-oh-oh, I’m still alive\nAh-ah-ah, say it plain\nOh-oh-oh, rain, rain, rain\n\n[Final Chorus]\nI don’t belong where the harvest is high\nI don’t belong, but I still arrive\nHey-oh, hey-oh, carry me through\nIf I’m the field, what grew in you?\nI don’t belong—say it plain, say it slow\nI don’t belong, but I won’t let go\nAh-ah, oh-oh, under the blue\nIf I’m the field, what grew in you?\n\n[Outro]\nThe gate stays shut, the morning starts\nThe ground remembers every heart\nAh-ah, oh-oh, I walk on through\nNo field can tell me what to do",
