      "lyric": "[Verse 1]\nI kept the line loose, kept the reel slow\nSalt on my lip where the cold winds blow\nYou said, “Let it run,” so I let it run\nThen the silver turned and the fight was done\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nOh, I know, I know, I know\nSome things leave before you let them go\nOh, I know, I know, I know\nEmpty hands still learn the shape of hope\n\n[Chorus]\nGone on the turn, gone on the turn\nBurn in my palm where the bright line burned\nGone on the turn, gone on the turn\nI had your weight, then I had none\n(Ah-ah, none, none)\nGone on the turn, gone on the turn\nNo hard words, just the lesson learned\nGone on the turn, gone on the turn\nI had your weight, then I had none\n\n[Verse 2]\nThe hook came back with a piece of blue\nA little bright thread, but nothing of you\nI laughed once, then I watched the tide\nCarry my almost to the other side\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nOh, I know, I know, I know\nSome things leave before you let them go\nOh, I know, I know, I know\nEmpty hands still learn the shape of hope\n\n[Chorus]\nGone on the turn, gone on the turn\nBurn in my palm where the bright line burned\nGone on the turn, gone on the turn\nI had your weight, then I had none\n(Ah-ah, none, none)\nGone on the turn, gone on the turn\nNo hard words, just the lesson learned\nGone on the turn, gone on the turn\nI had your weight, then I had none\n\n[Bridge]\nLet it go, let it go, let the water close\nLet it go, let it go, that is how it goes\nI won’t curse the sea, I won’t curse the dawn\nI’ll wind the line and carry on\n(Keep on, keep on)\n\n[Final Chorus]\nGone on the turn, gone on the turn\nBurn in my palm where the bright line burned\nGone on the turn, gone on the turn\nI had your weight, then I had none\n(Ah-ah, none, none)\nGone on the turn, gone on the turn\nNo hard words, just the lesson learned\nGone on the turn, gone on the turn\nI had your weight, then I had none\n\n[Outro]\nGone on the turn\nI wind the line\nGone on the turn\nI’ll be fine\n(Ah-ah, I’ll be fine)",
