      "describe": "While keeping things compelling, write reverently prosed, emotive, and cathartic lyrics about something that would make the person with lived experience feel stubborn awe where the lyrics have exceptional Meter, Rhyme, repetition, and Rhythm in the spirit of trance while considering an apt metaphor, \"turn of phrase\", colloquialism, or idiom leaving the person with lived experience emotionally compelled by the lyrics that one cannot help but sing along due to the vowel juxtaposition even if sometimes those vowels are part of apt vocalese, all while reducing to the most poignant emotionality. To speak in a different voice or add vocal effect write within (). subtly vector the lyrics against a single reference event you creatively select from maritime history but ultimately the lyrics are only beholden to themselves. Get unsparing with this one.",
      "style": "Trance, cinematic vocal trance with a clean club mix, wide delay throws, intimate breathy low-register lead vocal with layered octave doubles and breathy vocalese between phrases, minor-key arpeggiated synths, vast sub-bass and four-on-the-floor pulse, gradual tension and release from restrained verses into a cathartic anthemic chorus with choir-like harmonies, 126 BPM\n\nTake 2: Cinematic trance with crisp sidechain, long reverb tails, and gradual filter lifts; driving four-on-the-floor pulse, deep rolling sub-bass, wide minor-key supersaw chords, glassy arpeggio ostinato, restrained vocal chops; intimate low male lead expanding into stacked communal harmonies; tense verses opening to a cathartic anthemic chorus and powerful final release",
      "lyric": "— TAKE 1 —\n\n[Verse 1]\nSalt in the seam, iron under my tongue\nThe cold took the names of the old and the young\nI held to the rail while the black water climbed\nOne hand on the night, one hand on the line\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nAnd oh—when the whole world rolled away\nI heard my heart refuse to pray\nNot for a shore, not for a sign\nJust one more breath, just one more time\n\n[Chorus]\nCarry me, carry me, hard sea, carry me\nBreak every promise but leave me my name\nOh-ah, I rise where the deep would bury me\nNo shore can own me, no storm can erase me\nCarry me, carry me, merciless blue\nI lost what I was, but I came back as true\nAh-ah, through the black, through the bitter foam\nI was not saved—I made it home\n\n[Verse 2]\nThe mast bent low like a penitent spine\nThe moon wore a bruise at the edge of the brine\nBelow us, the drowned kept knocking in time\nAbove us, the stars would not testify\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nSo I gave the dark what the dark had won\nThen counted the waves till the counting was done\nNo saint in the spray, no hand from above\nJust bone against water, and stubborn love\n\n[Chorus]\nCarry me, carry me, hard sea, carry me\nBreak every promise but leave me my name\nOh-ah, I rise where the deep would bury me\nNo shore can own me, no storm can erase me\nCarry me, carry me, merciless blue\nI lost what I was, but I came back as true\nAh-ah, through the black, through the bitter foam\nI was not saved—I made it home\n\n[Bridge]\n(Stay—stay—stay)\nIf grief is an anchor, let it drag behind\nIf fear is a compass, I’ll turn it aside\nThe sea took the vessel, the years, and the crew\nBut every last wave brought me nearer to you\n\n[Final Chorus]\nCarry me, carry me, hard sea, carry me\nBreak every promise but leave me my name\nOh-ah, I rise where the deep would bury me\nNo shore can own me, no storm can erase me\nCarry me, carry me, merciless blue\nI lost what I was, but I came back as true\nAh-ah, through the black, through the bitter foam\nI was not saved—I made it home\n\n[Outro]\nAh-ah, I made it home\nOh-oh, I made it home\nThe sea knows my name\nThe sea knows my name\n\n— TAKE 2 —\n\n[Intro]\nAh—ah, oh—oh\nHold fast, hold fast\n\n[Verse 1]\nYou came back with the salt in your eyes,\nWith a torn blue thread where the daylight lies;\nNo harbor bell, no hand, no shore,\nJust your name in the oarlock, asking for more.\n\nThe sea took count of the ones you knew,\nLeft one red thread and a sky gone blue;\nYou said, \"I rowed till the dark grew thin—\"\nI said, \"You’re here. Let the breath begin.\"\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nAnd if the water keeps calling your name,\nLet it call—let it call in vain;\nThere are wounds that refuse to close,\nThere are hearts that refuse to go.\n\n[Chorus]\nRow, row—through the mouth of the night,\nOh, your blood is a stubborn light;\nLow, low—where the black tides roll,\nYou brought back a breathing soul.\n\nSing, sing—let the dead hear true,\nI was lost, but I came to you;\nWave, wave—let the whole world know:\nWhat the sea can take, we don’t owe.\n\n(Ah-ah, oh-oh, carry me home)\n(Ah-ah, oh-oh, I am not gone)\n\n[Verse 2]\nThere was rope on your palms like a rosary,\nThere was frost in your beard, there was no apology;\nYou had learned what the brave men learn—\nA match is a sun when the mast won’t burn.\n\nYou laughed at the lie that the deep is fair,\nAt the old salt prayer in the freezing air;\nThen you kissed the cup, then you drank it slow,\nFor the mouths beneath us, the ones below.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nAnd if the water keeps calling your name,\nLet it call—let it call in vain;\nThere are wounds that refuse to close,\nThere are hearts that refuse to go.\n\n[Chorus]\nRow, row—through the mouth of the night,\nOh, your blood is a stubborn light;\nLow, low—where the black tides roll,\nYou brought back a breathing soul.\n\nSing, sing—let the dead hear true,\nI was lost, but I came to you;\nWave, wave—let the whole world know:\nWhat the sea can take, we don’t owe.\n\n[Bridge]\nNo clean hands, no holy calm,\nJust a pulse beneath your battered palm;\nNo grand fate, no silver sign,\nOnly your breath answering mine.\n\nSo bite the rope and name the cost,\nCount every mile, count every lost;\nIf grief is a tide, then grief may rise—\nBut it will not have your eyes.\n\n(Building vocalese: ah-ah-ah, oh-oh-oh)\n\n[Final Chorus]\nRow, row—through the mouth of the night,\nOh, your blood is a stubborn light;\nLow, low—where the black tides roll,\nYou brought back a breathing soul.\n\nSing, sing—let the dead hear true,\nI was lost, but I came to you;\nWave, wave—let the whole world know:\nWhat the sea can take, we don’t owe.\n\nRow, row—when the morning breaks,\nCarry all that the living take;\nHold, hold—though the old world bends,\nWe are more than the sea intends.\n\n[Outro]\n(Ah-ah, oh-oh, carry me home)\n(Ah-ah, oh-oh, I am not gone)\nHold fast, hold fast—\nI am not gone.",
