      "describe": "While keeping things compelling, write bluntly prosed, emotive, and cathartic lyrics about something that would make the person with lived experience feel unearned envy where the lyrics have exceptional Meter, Rhyme, repetition, and Rhythm in the spirit of ambient while considering an apt metaphor, \"turn of phrase\", colloquialism, or idiom leaving the person with lived experience emotionally compelled by the lyrics that one cannot help but sing along due to the vowel juxtaposition even if sometimes those vowels are part of apt vocalese, all while reducing to the most poignant emotionality. To speak in a different voice or add vocal effect write within (). subtly vector the lyrics against a single reference event you creatively select from textile work but ultimately the lyrics are only beholden to themselves. Get unsparing with this one.",
      "style": "ambient indie folk, haunting minimalist arrangement, hypnotic rhythmic acoustic fingerpicking, soft ethereal male vocal, tape hiss, intimate dry mix\n\nTake 2: variety 1/4, ambient art-pop ballad, slow suspended pulse, felt piano, bowed glass tones, low sub drone, intimate close-miked lead vocal, restrained verses opening into a wide aching chorus, sparse vocalese between phrases, long tail reverb, clear consonants, warm low mids, gradual cathartic swell, unresolved final cadence",
      "lyric": "— TAKE 1 —\n\n[Intro]\n(hushed breath)\nPull the thread, pull the thread...\nThread the needle, feel the tension.\n(soft vocalise)\nAh, ooh, eye...\n\n[Verse 1]\nYou built the loom, you grew the flax\nYou bled the dye, you paid the tax\nYou spun the spool through cold and pain\nI took the cloth, I wiped the rain\nThe weave is tight, the pattern true\nI wear the coat that bled through you\nI walk the cold, I feel no frost\nYou count the years, you count the cost\n\n[Chorus]\n(whispered double)\nI wear your warp, I wear your weft\nYou have the hands, but nothing left\n(singing)\nOh, loom and line, oh, seam and fray\nYou spun the night, I took the day\nAh, seam to seam, oh, thread by thread\nYou made the sheet, I warm the bed\n\n[Verse 2]\nThe selvage holds, the border stays\nI wrap your work around my days\nUnearned, clean, soft on the skin\nYou stayed outside, I walked right in\nA simple twist, an easy fold\nI didn't spin, but I hold the gold\n(vocalise)\nOoh, ah, eye, seam and sky...\n\n[Chorus]\nI wear your warp, I wear your weft\nYou have the hands, but nothing left\nOh, loom and line, oh, seam and fray\nYou spun the night, I took the day\nAh, seam to seam, oh, thread by thread\nYou made the sheet, I warm the bed\n\n[Outro]\n(fading vocalese)\nAh... ooh...\nUnspooled, untouched.\nI warm the bed.\n(soft breath out)\n\n— TAKE 2 —\n\n[Verse 1]\nYou got the dress I cut by hand\nThe one that fit my shaking plan\nI pinned the hem, I chose the thread\nThen watched you wear the life I said\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI made it clean\nI made it last\nI made a future from the past\n\n[Chorus]\nAnd I envy you\nI envy you\nNot for the silk, not for the room\nI envy what you never knew\nI envy you\nI envy you\nYou get to call the wound brand-new\nI get the proof of what I drew\n\n[Verse 2]\nYour mother cried, your father smiled\nYou held the veil like something wild\nI stood behind the folding screen\nWith every hidden stitch between\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI bit my tongue\nI kept it neat\nI let your happiness leave my feet\n\n[Chorus]\nAnd I envy you\nI envy you\nNot for the silk, not for the room\nI envy what you never knew\nI envy you\nI envy you\nYou get to call the wound brand-new\nI get the proof of what I drew\n\n[Bridge]\nNo, I don’t want your borrowed praise\nNo, I don’t want your wedding days\nI want one hour untouched by me\nOne thing that does not carry my name\n\n[Break]\nAh-ah, ooh-ah\nAh-ah, ooh-ah\nCut the cord, cut the cord\nLet the clean edge hurt\n\n[Final Chorus]\nAnd I envy you\nI envy you\nYou wear the dream I dragged it through\nYou call it love; I call it true\nI envy you\nI envy you\nThe cruelest part is this is new\nThe cruelest part is I made you\n\n[Outro]\nPull the thread\nLet it bleed\nLeave one seam\nI cannot see\nAh-ah, ooh-ah\nI envy you",
