      "style": "rock, emotionally cathartic, urgent midtempo groove, overdriven electric guitars, muscular live drums, melodic bass, tense verses opening into a huge sing-along chorus, dynamic stop-start bridge, gritty expressive lead vocal, stacked gang harmonies, punchy modern mix with raw human edges",
      "lyric": "[Verse 1]\nYou wore the blame like a borrowed coat\nButtoned it tight at the throat\nEvery room had a verdict ready\nEvery hand said, hold steady\nBut the floor gave way beneath your feet\nAnd the old lie missed its beat\nYou found one breath in the wreckage there\nOne small no in the poisoned air\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nOh, let it rise, let it rise\nFrom the ribs to the rafters tonight\n\n[Chorus]\nI am not the wound they named\nI am not the debt unpaid\nI am the spark beneath the rain\nThe open door, the windowpane\nSay it loud till the silence goes\nSay it twice so the whole world knows\nI was bent, I was bruised, I was pulled apart\nBut I came back with a beating heart\n\n[Verse 2]\nThey drew a line through the family name\nStamped it clean and called it shame\nYou learned the weight of a locked-up tongue\nAnd the cost of the songs unsung\nThen a match struck hard in the winter dark\nNot a flame, just a stubborn spark\nYou held it close through the bitter cold\nTill the little light turned bold\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nOh, let it rise, let it rise\nFrom the ribs to the rafters tonight\n\n[Chorus]\nI am not the wound they named\nI am not the debt unpaid\nI am the spark beneath the rain\nThe open door, the windowpane\nSay it loud till the silence goes\nSay it twice so the whole world knows\nI was bent, I was bruised, I was pulled apart\nBut I came back with a beating heart\n\n[Bridge]\nNo crown, no cure, no clean escape\nJust both hands on the shape I make\nIf the past comes knocking, let it knock\nI have learned the language of the lock\n(hey-ah, hey-ah)\nI have learned the language of the lock\n\n[Final Chorus]\nI am not the wound they named\nI am not the debt unpaid\nI am the spark beneath the rain\nThe open door, the windowpane\nSay it loud till the silence goes\nSay it twice so the whole world knows\nI was bent, I was bruised, I was pulled apart\nBut I came back with a beating heart\n\n[Outro]\nWith a beating heart\nWith a beating heart\nOh, I came back\nI came back",
