      "describe": "While keeping things compelling, write [INSERT adverb] prosed, emotive, and cathartic lyrics about something that would make the person with lived experience feel [INSERT up to 3 word, non-specific, idea] where the lyrics have exceptional Meter, Rhyme, repetition, and Rhythm in the spirit of techno while considering an apt metaphor, \"turn of phrase\", colloquialism, or idiom leaving the person with lived experience emotionally compelled by the lyrics that one cannot help but sing along due to the vowel juxtaposition even if sometimes those vowels are part of apt vocalese, all while reducing to the most poignant emotionality. To speak in a different voice or add vocal effect write within (). subtly vector the lyrics against a single reference event you creatively select from [INSERT field of human work or history] but ultimately the lyrics are only beholden to themselves. Get [INSERT compelling term] with this one.",
      "style": "techno, driving four-on-the-floor pulse, hypnotic acid bass, taut syncopated percussion, dark warehouse atmosphere, intimate low male vocal, clipped verse phrasing, explosive sing-along hook, vowel-led vocalese, tension-building risers, cathartic breakdown, polished club mix, variety 1/4",
      "lyric": "[Verse 1]\nI signed my name in borrowed rain\nBuilt a room inside the flame\nEvery door said, “Not today”\nSo I learned the lock, I walked away\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nOh-ah, over and over\nNo more weight upon my shoulder\nEh-oh, easy, let it go\nWhat I lose is what I know\n\n[Chorus]\nI’m not your almost, not your maybe\nNot the hand you hold when you’re afraid, see\nTurn the key, let the old world close\nI am more than the wound I chose\n\nI’m not your almost, not your maybe\nNo more waiting to be saved, baby\nAh-ah, I rise, I rise alone\nI take my name, I take my home\n\n[Verse 2]\nIn the night shift, under steel\nI found out what was real\nOne small spark beneath the floor\nSaid, “You don’t work there anymore”\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nOh-ah, over and over\nNo more weight upon my shoulder\nEh-oh, easy, let it go\nWhat I lose is what I know\n\n[Chorus]\nI’m not your almost, not your maybe\nNot the hand you hold when you’re afraid, see\nTurn the key, let the old world close\nI am more than the wound I chose\n\nI’m not your almost, not your maybe\nNo more waiting to be saved, baby\nAh-ah, I rise, I rise alone\nI take my name, I take my home\n\n[Bridge]\n(half-spoken, close)\nCount the breaths, count the cost\nCount the years I thought were lost\nOne for grief and one for grace\nOne to meet my own face\n\n[Instrumental]\nAh-ah-ah, eh-oh-oh\nAh-ah-ah, let it go\n\n[Final Chorus]\nI’m not your almost, not your maybe\nNot the hand you hold when you’re afraid, see\nTurn the key, let the old world close\nI am more than the wound I chose\n\nI’m not your almost, not your maybe\nNo more waiting to be saved, baby\nAh-ah, I rise, I rise alone\nI take my name, I take my home\n\n[Outro]\nI take my name\nI take my home\nAh-ah, I rise\nI rise alone",
